  "notes": "Entirely business-type entity; College column used (Foundations component unit excluded). Receipts/disbursements from Statement of Revenues, Expenses and Changes in Net Position (p3); receipts = operating revenues + nonoperating revenues excluding interest expense (38,062 shown as disbursement). other_financing 13,993,545 = gain on disposal 19,409 + capital appropriations 13,974,136 (p4), computed as printed total other revenues. Roll-forward: 65,529,029 + 40,718,985 - 42,413,949 + 13,993,545 = 77,827,610. Statement lists expenses by object only; mapped to support services with review. General Fund budgetary schedule (pp7-9) recorded in detail; budget-basis revenue schedule's '(Add to)/use cash reserves' balancing line (-4,606,893) recorded as other financing printed inside the revenue total (32,544,068, p7). Depreciation disbursement categorized other (non-cash, no function). No budget column in schedules. Deferred inflows 520,148 appear as printed total only. Read pages 1-9 of 9",
  "decision_needed": [
    {
      "question": "State/local capital appropriations of 13,993,545 are recorded as business-type other financing, not receipts. The cash flow statement (p5) shows 4,912,726 of 'Property taxes - Capital Improvement Fund', so much of it may be capital-levy property tax. Should it count as receipts (property tax / state aid)?",
      "amount": 13993545,
